<title>UK: Korea Exchange Bank sets $200 million one-year FRN. [CORRECTED 09:35 GMT]</title>
<headline>Korea Exchange Bank sets $200 million one-year FRN. [CORRECTED 09:35 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects amount in headline from $100 million to $200 million)</p>
<p>The following floating-rate issue was announced by lead manager Nomura.</p>
<p> BORROWER   KOREA EXCHANGE BANK</p>
<p> AMT    $200 MLN	BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY	 DEC.97</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN     10 BP     PAY DATE    24.DEC.96</p>
<p> LAST MOODY =	   ISS PRICE  99.952    FULL FEES   5 BP</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   =	   REOFFER    99.952</p>
<p> LISTING  LUX  DENOMS (K) 1-10-100 SALE LIMITS US/UK/JP/KR/DE/FR</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  KOREA     TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    2.5 BP    SELL CONC  2.5 BP    PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
